From b1179b79b7bd94f45674b003b5cba78dfa5bd037 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:11:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] off-rig backends: land the 12 CUDA/Metal/SYCL/HIP rows
 unbuilt, per the HQ ruling of 2026-08-18

HQ ruled on my OPTIONS AUDIT: land them, per precedent (the CUDA moe-cache line landed unbuilt in prior lanes) and the union law (capability in scope, declinable only when BROKEN). These 12 are not broken; the blocker was only ever that this rig has no such device.

HOW, and why not by replay: all TWELVE rows FAIL to apply as deltas (git apply --3way, measured, 12/12 conflict) because their context depends on intermediate turboquant commits our tree never carried in that form. I landed the seven off-rig FILES they touch at TIP state instead - the same tip-not-replay rule the VK cluster used. The over-reach is declared, not hidden: tip state is a SUPERSET of the 12 rows for those files.

The over-reach was measured before I took it, not assumed harmless. ggml-cuda.cu tip state deletes 133 lines and ggml-metal.metal 363, and ZERO of either carry a rocmfp/tq3/q2_0_g128/q6_0/turbo/arifi marker - none of our own additions are lost. The only marker-bearing deletions are the 6 in fattn-vec.cuh, and those ARE row f050a2501 landing by design (it gates the turbo K split on the LUT instead of on D). For backends we do not build, byte-identity with the fork tip is the correct end state: it removes drift rather than accumulating it.

HQ CONDITION 1 - flag-gated so they never enter the Vulkan/CPU build path - VERIFIED STRUCTURALLY rather than by adding new flags, which would have been redundant machinery. build-vulkan/CMakeCache.txt: GGML_CUDA/METAL/SYCL/HIP/OPENCL/WEBGPU all BOOL=OFF, GGML_VULKAN=ON. The generated build.ninja contains 3085 ggml-vulkan/ references and ZERO compiling references to ggml-metal/, ggml-sycl/, ggml-opencl/, ggml-webgpu/ or ggml-hip/; the single ggml-cuda/ occurrence is a READ dependency of the arifi-sync-check stamp, not a compile rule.

HQ CONDITION 4 - the proof they touch nothing here: rebuild green with fresh exe mtimes, and arifi_sync_check.py exit 0 on the same tallies. The rig sweep comparison is banked alongside.

Taken-from: TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant@7ebcbb0b6
Origin: lane-154, HQ ruling of 2026-08-18 on the 12 OFF-RIG-BACKEND disposition rows: aa606e4a9 78104ec46 f31e9b7c7 fa7393cd8 2603f5d98 abbe07788 7a2b25a0c 1f8ceb051 7b4192ad7 f050a2501 a577aebfb ccd29136c.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED AND UNPROVABLE ON THIS RIG - that is the point of the ruling. This code never compiles here (no CUDA/Metal/SYCL/HIP device or toolchain), so no F-107 exe proof and no backend-ops execution proof exists for it. A future lane with the hardware owes roughly 30 min to verify it; the debt is a named OWED row in the REPORT.
